CRT presentation in mission.css adapts visual concepts from cool-retro-term,
copyright (c) 2013-2021 Filippo Scognamiglio, https://github.com/Swordfish90/cool-retro-term
Upstream source commit: 1394ce82fa53d2a87d5adc4d99f9eeba598ea53d

The browser adaptation ports the static shader's quadratic radial coordinate
distortion, its left/center/right RGB blend weights, and its static noise and
edge shading. `setupCRTEffect()` in `mission.js` applies the upstream
`distortCoordinates()` equation to a small transparent raster overlay and
derives the scanline, noise, and vignette alpha. CSS maps the shader's channel
weights to restrained colored DOM text shadows. Text and controls remain live
DOM, so they stay accessible and readable without a shader-capable renderer.
This is a responsive browser adaptation, not a pixel-identical GLSL render.
Source reference: `app/shaders/terminal_static.frag`, especially
`distortCoordinates()` and the `CRT_RGB_SHIFT` channel blend. The browser
program does not include or execute upstream Qt/QML or GLSL. The upstream
project is licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later; its complete license text is
included in LICENSE.

